(E'966508e4-5acf-5f16-b7aa-c7d26a2fbb5d'::uuid,E'8911a053-1b14-587f-b906-c0fb2adaf7f3'::uuid,E'482607e8-b88e-5f6a-97d2-d5225fcfa899'::uuid,'primary','partially_met','prefilled_iat',E'[B7.2] DR: 10-Yr Plan says trained personnel staff the EOC but need ICS all levels, EOC Management and MDM training.\n\n[B6.4] DR: 10-Yr Plan says a donations/relief system is established. DR (doc review 6 Nov 2026): SP Res. 2024-102 (2 Apr 2024; file named "SP RESOLUTION NO. 2024-1027") grants the Mayor or OIC Mayor omnibus authority to accept donations of perishable goods and goods given during or after calamities and to sign deeds of donation. Volunteers: CPR-RIMT MOA (SP Res. 2023-347). No donations-handling SOP in the set.',E'[B7.2] Provisional.\n\n[B6.4] Provisional. The legal authority to accept calamity donations exists (SP Res. 2024-102), but no SOP for receiving, recording, storing, distributing and reporting donations, or for registering spontaneous volunteers, was sighted. Correct the file name in the Vault (2024-1027 vs 2024-102).',E'[B7.2] Complete EOC Management and ICS courses for all EOC staff.\n\n[B6.4] Write the donations and volunteer SOP under SP Res. 2024-102: intake desk, deed of donation, logging, warehousing with CSWD/CGSO, distribution records, FDP posting; spontaneous-volunteer registration and tasking through the EOC.'),
